A frontmatter delimiter may be followed by whitespace (`--- `), and the block may close with
YAML's document end marker `...` instead of `---`. Either way the fields are the header and the
closing line is no setext heading underline, so the body's headings start after it.
== args
input/trailing-space.md
input/dots.md
== file input/trailing-space.md escaped
--- \n\
title: trailing space\n\
---\t\n\
# H1\n\
== file input/dots.md
---
title: dots
...
# H1
== stdout
input/trailing-space.md (4 lines)
title: "trailing space"
[L4-L4] # H1

input/dots.md (4 lines)
title: "dots"
[L4-L4] # H1
== stderr
== exit 0
